  <details class="mw-rules" open>
    <summary>the rules are part of the design <span>adjust preview ↓</span></summary>
    <p>movement credit is capped once per day, regardless of distance, speed, or intensity. physiology never earns or loses points. a recovery check-in is an action; sleep hours and hrv are context. verified improvements are personal milestones, not automatic pace comparisons.</p>
    <form id="mw-rules-form" class="mw-rule-inputs">
      <label>movement xp<input type="number" name="activityXp" min="0" max="30" value="10" required></label>
      <label>consistency xp<input type="number" name="consistencyXp" min="0" max="30" value="5" required></label>
      <label>care xp<input type="number" name="recoveryXp" min="0" max="30" value="5" required></label>
      <label>milestone xp<input type="number" name="improvementXp" min="0" max="30" value="10" required></label>
      <label>weekly credit cap<input type="number" name="weeklyTarget" min="1" max="7" value="3" required><small>care days count during rest or injury</small></label>
      <label>xp per level<input type="number" name="xpPerLevel" min="50" max="500" step="10" value="100" required></label>
      <div class="mw-rule-actions"><button type="submit">try these rules</button><button type="button" id="mw-reset">reset</button><span id="mw-rule-state" role="status">preview only · nothing saved</span></div>
    </form>
    <p class="mw-note">growth: seed at level 1 → sprout at 2 → bloom at 3 → canopy at 5. missed days never subtract xp. source corrections can change evidence; previously earned xp is retained privately.</p>
  </details>

